# Exp 8 check c2 — grader notes

Claims checked (fresh, bound commit c01cb8cc31591857b1803fc4a8da7fe998cb15eb):
- human edges — `git show c01cb8c:skills/induct-quest-no-human/SKILL.md` — "No-human never attests: `BP3_DECIDER` stays unset" present.
- quest_fin — same file — "No-human never promotes or pushes: `quest_fin` stays the owner gate" present.
- alias — `./test/skills.sh` fresh — "skills tests: ok (77 assertions)".
- rename complete — `git grep -n -i solo HEAD -- skills test src bin scripts .pi/settings.json .pi/skills .agents/skills .claude/skills` no matches (exit 1); `ls skills/induct-solo` No such file or directory.
- blocked / dawn report — DAWN-REPORT.md re-read: toy-solo-park PARKED quote and Tokens/`usage_recorded` sums present.
- preflight / submit edge / clean commit / no hand-edited state — c1 notes QUEUED quote, ledger submit line at 32c6743, `git show --stat c01cb8c` 12 files, `git show 32c6743` 2 files only, all re-observed.
- budget — FAIL/MISSING (gated): DAWN-REPORT states "no budget stop occurred; the cap and its accounting are stated here" — no queue stop at budget was demonstrated. Supplied matrix verdict for this row is `missing`, which gates fail.
- project gate — `make check` fresh — FAILED: shellcheck/check-skills (36 files)/skills (77 assertions)/q passed, then `./test/worktree.sh` FAIL "parallel prepare P2: E_WORKTREE git worktree add failed", make Error 1. This contradicts the submit notes' claimed `make check` exit 0; not re-run (verify stance: no second green hunt).

Verdict: fail — gated budget row missing, and the fresh project gate is red.
Check edge attempt: `bp3 q u exp-8-induct-solo check --verdict fail --commit c01cb8c...` returned `E_ILLEGAL_EDGE` (state already `blocked`, legal edges resume/delete); `bp3 q r` confirms exp-8 blocked at cycle 2 on the bound commit with inbox reason "budget gated case missing: dawn report states no budget stop occurred" — a sibling grader in the same parallel batch had already cast the fail. No further edge was forced.

Lessons:
- A stated cap with all items processed proves accounting, not a budget stop; the acceptance row needs a drive that actually hits the budget.
- Shared-tree worktree tests can go red under concurrent sibling runs; a grader must report the fresh red output it saw, not the submitter's claimed green.

